{"title":"2018 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part C","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2018 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <i>range</i> of a list of numbers is the difference between the largest number and the smallest number in the list. For example, the range of the list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7f8bc14cdd0631cafcfbbc1b5eff7c66c6b959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 5, 1, 6, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74dbf5a4d426fb8bb63d88ab4f21b351d2ee670c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5c1c9c5036ab328ac9dae49df704b943d89f68d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 2x^{2}, 6 + 4x^{2}, 6, 6 + 5x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"210\" height=\"20\" /> has a range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Determine the two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/e/60ea03b5fcdba626d0f3406ce61d14d65ee0d1df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cx^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"17\" /> is always positive for the real numbers if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd17f0410677a7953daee77fd09bd27d1e79f8a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + cx^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> must be higher as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> increases. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be the smallest value in the list, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/1770108522b669579307b36bdea932629afd979b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 5x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> must be the largest value in the list. The range of the list would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/4/cf4f03973d557b97d73722eb24ced826d199cb74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 5x^{2} - 6 = 5x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />, meaning:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/7/f6771b299fe83b1e2497d286abb6bf7403834e20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x^{2} = 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b981e4dd46277c06b49419bdfb8ecbdd63d1cad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{2} = \\frac{80}{5} = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b56339a1b9927cb97fa5445ff3d39882142efba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\pm \\sqrt{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f7d3b37412c07a4336ec32bbc9865f7e489925.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"55\" height=\"23\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/d/e9df95d3ae0fc2810e323e12800475d6c6c1682c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = -4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"71\" height=\"26\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018061944\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 67/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 302/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3087/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.509      1 2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%    6.509      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37102:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018061944 and revision id 286423. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}